WEBVTT

01:42.090 --> 01:43.090
Sai...

01:49.290 --> 01:51.990
You came into my dream

01:56.090 --> 01:56.790
Don't go

01:57.190 --> 01:58.190
Say something!

01:58.990 --> 01:59.790
Don't disappear!

02:00.490 --> 02:01.290
Sai...

02:27.590 --> 02:32.490
Road to Hokutohai

03:04.990 --> 03:06.190
Is Hikaru playing the board game?

03:08.890 --> 03:10.590
Huh? Did you say something?

03:11.390 --> 03:12.890
Hikaru is doing 'this' again?

03:13.290 --> 03:15.490
Yes, as soon as he came home...

03:15.790 --> 03:18.090
He said, I'm hungary, Ramen"...

03:18.490 --> 03:20.790
So I cooked it for him...

03:20.790 --> 03:22.790
And he finished it before I could blink and went to his room

03:24.690 --> 03:27.590
That child has been like that recently

03:35.790 --> 03:36.490
Sai...

03:37.290 --> 03:39.490
I'm at a pretty good pace these days

03:40.190 --> 03:42.090
I am continuausly winning the Honinbou matches

03:44.890 --> 03:46.590
I want to hurry up and compete against the experts

03:48.290 --> 03:49.890
I want to keep winning and winning

03:50.190 --> 03:51.190
and winning like this...

03:52.290 --> 03:52.990
And someday...

03:53.890 --> 03:54.890
Someday... You...

03:56.290 --> 03:56.790
Hikaru...?

03:58.690 --> 04:01.490
Hikaru, you have a phone call from the Go Institute

04:02.090 --> 04:02.990
Okay, I'm coming

04:09.490 --> 04:10.090
Hello?

04:10.590 --> 04:11.790
Shindou-Kun...

04:12.090 --> 04:14.290
I'm Kosemura from the publishing department of Japan's Go Institute

04:14.690 --> 04:16.840
I want to ask you something...

04:18.490 --> 04:20.690
Yes

04:22.690 --> 04:23.690
Huh? Hokutohai?

04:24.290 --> 04:26.290
Note: Ni = Nihon = Japan: Chuu = Chuugoku = Cina: Kan = Kankoku = Korea
Ni and Chuu and Kan junoir team competition?

04:27.890 --> 04:31.390
Japan, China and Korea junior team competition?

04:31.490 --> 04:33.390
Yeah, sounds like fun... Huh?

04:34.190 --> 04:35.490
He said it was at Hokutohai

04:36.890 --> 04:39.090
You must be under eighteen and there are three members per team

04:39.590 --> 04:40.390
I know

04:41.590 --> 04:43.890
Player selection preliminary matches start in April

04:44.390 --> 04:45.690
Do you think I can try out for it, too?

04:46.090 --> 04:47.290
I passed this year

04:48.190 --> 04:50.390
Isumi-san, Shindou just told you...

04:50.990 --> 04:52.190
That it's for under eighteen only

04:56.690 --> 04:59.190
It is.. Junior...

05:00.090 --> 05:03.490
Even though Isumi-san and Kodowaki-san can't enter this year...

05:03.890 --> 05:05.690
Honda-san is eighteen, right?

05:06.090 --> 05:08.090
That's right. Do you remember Su-Young?

05:08.390 --> 05:08.990
Su-Young?

05:09.990 --> 05:11.890
You mean the Korean boy we saw at the Go salon?

05:12.290 --> 05:15.790
The man at the publishing department said that he is a pro now

05:16.590 --> 05:18.590
He said he might be entering Hokutohai

05:20.090 --> 05:21.890
Korean teens are incredible

05:22.590 --> 05:25.090
Go Young-Ha is already at the top age of sixteen...

05:25.790 --> 05:26.890
China is the same...

05:27.990 --> 05:28.490
Well,

05:28.790 --> 05:30.490
Japan has Touya Akira...

05:31.090 --> 05:32.290
They have me too!

05:37.790 --> 05:41.190
I'm not planning on staring at the back side of Touya forever

05:43.990 --> 05:45.790
This is your only game this week?

05:46.090 --> 05:49.690
Yes. It's the Honinbou match, first preliminary final

05:50.790 --> 05:53.290
It's all wrong... You're completely pinched

05:53.690 --> 05:56.190
What are you talking about? I've reversed!

05:56.590 --> 05:57.890
I won by 1.5 moku

05:58.290 --> 06:01.490
Reverse was possible because the opponent's hand was too simple

06:02.290 --> 06:06.290
You're not thinking that you won because you played well, are you?

06:08.790 --> 06:11.390
Must you say it like that?

06:11.390 --> 06:13.190
That's the truth

06:13.490 --> 06:14.290
What?

06:14.290 --> 06:17.190
This game... I wouldn't have allowed a reverse if it was me

06:18.790 --> 06:19.690
If it was me

06:19.690 --> 06:21.990
I would've went in for the kill before you surrounded the middle

06:22.990 --> 06:24.390
If you can't take over the middle

06:24.790 --> 06:26.290
There's no way black could've won

06:27.090 --> 06:27.890
How about it?

06:27.890 --> 06:28.890
You can't reverse, can you?

06:29.990 --> 06:32.390
Just a minute, if it's me... I would change it like this

06:33.190 --> 06:35.490
In this case, you won't be able to do as you planned

06:35.890 --> 06:38.490
But then, you're giving up space on this side

06:39.290 --> 06:40.790
If the middle clears up

06:41.190 --> 06:44.190
It'll increase the number of moku you'll lose by... Let alone reversing

06:44.690 --> 06:48.890
No, if I destroy the white territory with the trigonal form here... It's not bad

06:48.890 --> 06:50.190
What's not bad!?

06:50.590 --> 06:52.590
How can you fight with this form?

06:52.590 --> 06:53.890
If it's me, I can fight!

06:54.290 --> 06:55.990
This trigonal form here is more than enough!

06:56.390 --> 06:59.190
They're always so violent...

07:01.090 --> 07:02.090
Why don't you just give up...

07:02.590 --> 07:03.690
You think I'm crazy?

07:08.690 --> 07:10.790
Acting like you're all that is only for now

07:11.490 --> 07:13.690
Someday.. I'll defeat you in an official match

07:15.490 --> 07:16.190
Just a minute,

07:16.790 --> 07:18.190
there are preliminary matches for Hokutohai

07:18.490 --> 07:20.590
You know the team competition, right?

07:21.490 --> 07:23.290
We might be able to have a match there

07:27.090 --> 07:30.190
That Hokutohai... I'm not in the preliminaries

07:31.790 --> 07:33.190
I've already been selected as a player

07:35.590 --> 07:36.590
Why is that?

07:36.890 --> 07:38.190
Why do you get out of it?!

07:38.590 --> 07:39.490
That's not fair!

07:40.790 --> 07:42.890
Even in other things...

07:42.890 --> 07:44.390
A person with good results recieves seed

07:44.790 --> 07:47.090
Akira-sensei enters the league matches, too

07:47.390 --> 07:48.290
Do you have more to say?

07:48.790 --> 07:49.390
Right, right...

07:49.790 --> 07:51.190
Shindou-Kun is shodan

07:51.490 --> 07:52.390
Do you understand?

07:54.690 --> 07:58.090
It's the difference between a person who enters the league matches and just a mere shodan...?

08:01.290 --> 08:01.990
Shindou?

08:02.690 --> 08:04.990
But it's not the difference in skills

08:05.290 --> 08:08.390
Hey, that's enough bragging!

08:09.690 --> 08:12.590
I'll definitely pass the preliminary match in April

08:13.290 --> 08:15.090
Until then... I won't be coming here

08:21.190 --> 08:22.190
It's four months away

08:23.090 --> 08:26.890
At that time, I will be a member of Japan's team... Just like you

08:35.690 --> 08:36.490
Superior...

08:36.790 --> 08:39.290
You know the Hokutohai our compay is sponsoring...?

08:40.190 --> 08:42.690
It's a big project to celebrate the stock list, right?

08:43.090 --> 08:44.290
Go is so boring...

08:44.590 --> 08:46.390
I wonder if it's going to be interesting for the people

08:46.890 --> 08:48.890
That's why I made it a team competition

08:49.390 --> 08:52.390
Japan verses China or prehaps Korea...

08:52.790 --> 08:54.990
Even the general people will take interest

08:55.490 --> 08:56.190
I see...

08:56.490 --> 08:57.390
I think they will

08:57.690 --> 09:01.290
National Rivalry competitions make your blood boil, just like the olympics

09:01.790 --> 09:03.790
I'm going to cheer for Japan, too!

09:04.090 --> 09:05.290
For Touya Akira

09:07.290 --> 09:09.790
It's surprising that you remember a player's name

09:10.290 --> 09:13.490
The security guards were talking about it yesterday

09:13.790 --> 09:15.890
That Touya Akira will show us something

09:16.190 --> 09:17.190
But...

09:17.190 --> 09:20.990
I heard Touya is the only one who might be able to defeat China or Korea

09:21.290 --> 09:22.390
There is one more

09:23.490 --> 09:24.390
Really?

09:24.690 --> 09:25.990
Then Japan can, too...?

09:26.290 --> 09:29.290
Even though we have him... There's only an expectation from the surroundings...

09:29.590 --> 09:31.590
His pro skills are zero

09:32.190 --> 09:32.990
Zero?

09:34.690 --> 09:35.890
Who is he?

09:36.390 --> 09:38.390
He's the one who became a pro in Kansai Go Institute

09:38.890 --> 09:41.390
He hasn't cut the start line as a pro yet

09:41.790 --> 09:43.890
Heh... From Kansai?

09:44.490 --> 09:46.390
Superior, you know so much

09:46.890 --> 09:50.190
Someone from the Kansai Go Institute told me over the phone...

09:51.190 --> 09:52.890
... That he is pretty good

09:54.290 --> 09:55.290
Now the two of you...

09:55.790 --> 09:57.090
Stand right about there

10:01.390 --> 10:02.290
What's wrong?

10:02.290 --> 10:04.190
You look stiff

10:05.590 --> 10:09.490
Don't be nervous just because you're the first player of the new shodan matches, Isumi-kun

10:10.090 --> 10:11.490
You're not used to the camera?

10:11.790 --> 10:14.690
You're not like the young people these days

10:15.390 --> 10:18.090
But even if you're nervous...

10:18.090 --> 10:21.590
An old man like me won't even be a match for you

10:21.890 --> 10:24.490
After all, aren't you the talented Go player who passed the Pro exam

10:24.490 --> 10:26.890
With a complete victory?

10:26.890 --> 10:28.490
No way...

10:29.290 --> 10:32.890
Wow... Kuwabara-sensei... Is already giving him pressure...

10:33.790 --> 10:36.490
You look skinny, but very firm...

10:36.490 --> 10:38.690
Do you play sports?

10:38.690 --> 10:39.590
N...No.

10:48.990 --> 10:52.390
I can't believe Isumi-san's New Shodan match's opponent is Kuwabara-sensei

10:52.790 --> 10:53.690
I'm looking forward to it

10:55.490 --> 10:56.390
Shindou-Kun...

11:03.090 --> 11:04.790
Shindou Hikaru... Shodan, right?

11:15.090 --> 11:16.190
Kadowaki-san?

11:17.690 --> 11:19.890
You remember my name. I'm glad

11:20.790 --> 11:22.990
Did you see me in the Weekly Go?

11:23.000 --> 11:27.690
Yes, I was surprised when I saw the pictures of the successful candidates from the pro exam

11:27.990 --> 11:31.690
I remembered that you're the one I played against when I was an Insei

11:33.390 --> 11:34.690
You still remembered?

11:35.290 --> 11:36.290
It's an honor

11:37.790 --> 11:42.090
Truthfully... I wanted to take the pro exam in the same year as you did

11:43.790 --> 11:48.090
At that time, I wanted to warm up so I asked you to play a game with me

11:48.390 --> 11:53.390
But... I got beaten by you, an Insei

11:53.990 --> 11:55.490
So, I realized my incapability

11:55.790 --> 12:00.090
and postponed it for a year... Thinking that I wasn't good enough like this

12:02.390 --> 12:04.090
Even though I had the confidence to pass it...

12:04.390 --> 12:07.290
I didn't have the confidence to defeat a Go player like yourself

12:07.790 --> 12:09.290
Thinking that I should look further up abit...

12:09.690 --> 12:11.790
And choose a higher goal

12:12.590 --> 12:14.690
You, at the time

12:14.690 --> 12:16.690
Were incredible enough to make a conceited person like me feel that way

12:20.890 --> 12:22.790
I wasn't the one who played that time...

12:24.690 --> 12:27.190
The one who played at that time was... Sai

12:31.690 --> 12:32.390
However...

12:32.690 --> 12:35.490
You recorded three losses in the pro exam

12:36.990 --> 12:41.290
And you were defeated shamefully in Touya Kouyou's new shodan match

12:41.890 --> 12:44.990
Plus, after you became a pro...
You continuosly forfeited...

12:46.890 --> 12:47.790
Hey now.

12:52.790 --> 12:53.990
What the hell went wrong?

12:55.790 --> 12:57.190
What are you doing...

12:57.890 --> 12:58.790
Shindou?

13:00.590 --> 13:01.490
He's late

13:02.290 --> 13:05.690
He did say he was going to come and watch Isumi-san's new shodan match

13:06.390 --> 13:08.390
Kadowaki-san isn't here yet either

13:09.790 --> 13:12.790
Honda-san had six losses in the pro exam, right?

13:13.290 --> 13:15.490
You surely passed well with that kind of a record

13:15.890 --> 13:17.390
Isumi-san has a complete victory and...

13:17.690 --> 13:20.090
Kadowaki-san lost only once to Isumi-san

13:20.790 --> 13:23.490
The two of them won everything this year

13:23.890 --> 13:25.690
So the rest of us had confusing fights

13:33.990 --> 13:34.890
He's not coming....

13:40.890 --> 13:41.690
You know, Hokutohai...

13:41.990 --> 13:43.690
I heard Touya has already been selected as a representative, right?

13:44.090 --> 13:45.590
If they took skills into consideration

13:45.590 --> 13:47.690
I think I should be selected aswell...

13:48.490 --> 13:49.390
In order to do that

13:49.690 --> 13:53.190
Anyone under eighteen should be difficult to divide since their skills aren't great

13:53.890 --> 13:54.590
Isn't that right?

13:54.990 --> 13:57.990
Honda-san, Who became a pro this year, is qualified...

13:58.690 --> 14:00.090
If you include the pros

14:00.590 --> 14:03.290
I heard that there was an up and coming player from Kansai Go Institute

14:04.190 --> 14:05.290
Kansai Go Institute?

14:05.690 --> 14:06.490
I see

14:06.790 --> 14:08.590
Players are coming from the Kansai Go Institute, too

14:11.390 --> 14:12.190
Isumi-san is playing

14:12.590 --> 14:13.190
It started

14:14.090 --> 14:15.990
He has a diferent feeling than Shindou last year

14:16.590 --> 14:19.190
He... Took twenty minutes to play the first stone

14:21.890 --> 14:23.890
Did something happen to... Shindou...?

14:24.590 --> 14:26.090
Kadowaki-san isn't coming either...

14:27.490 --> 14:29.890
It's impossible that they'd be playing each other...

14:30.490 --> 14:31.790
It's not that they know each other...

14:34.290 --> 14:35.290
Know each other?

14:36.190 --> 14:38.290
They don't know each other?

14:38.290 --> 14:40.090
That's right!
That was Shindou!

14:41.190 --> 14:41.690
Honda-san?

14:42.190 --> 14:43.590
That was about Shindou...

14:44.190 --> 14:46.890
At that time.
What Kadowaki-san was mumbling about...

14:48.290 --> 14:51.890
Ooshima... Fuku... Honda...

14:54.490 --> 14:57.190
Ones he lost to.. Were these three

14:58.490 --> 14:59.790
I can't believe it after all...

15:01.390 --> 15:03.390
Ooshima, Fuku, Honda...

15:04.790 --> 15:07.990
Those are the opponents Shindou lost to in the last year's pro exam

15:08.390 --> 15:09.590
You remember that well

15:10.890 --> 15:12.090
Because at that time...

15:12.390 --> 15:14.890
Me and Honda-san competed against him until the end, too

15:16.290 --> 15:18.190
Then, was that about Shindou, too?

15:18.190 --> 15:19.890
Waya, you know something, too?

15:20.290 --> 15:22.590
What...? Everyone is talking about Shindou, Shindou...

15:23.390 --> 15:29.390
I read a rumor about Kadowaki-san postponing the pro exam for a year on the net

15:29.890 --> 15:33.690
The reason for that was... Because he lost to a kid

15:34.590 --> 15:35.690
That kid was...

15:36.490 --> 15:37.290
Shindou?

15:50.590 --> 15:52.690
The reason you lost three matches in the pro exam...

15:52.990 --> 15:56.390
I thought it could've been because your skills have ups and downs, since you're still a kid

15:56.990 --> 15:59.990
But your skills aren't at that kind of level

16:03.590 --> 16:04.690
With that one game

16:05.090 --> 16:10.290
I even felt respect towards you, who is twelve years younger than I

16:11.190 --> 16:11.990
Isn't that funny?

16:15.590 --> 16:19.890
However, I feel as though that could've been a dream or an illusion right now

16:21.990 --> 16:23.890
What should I do about...

16:24.390 --> 16:26.190
The big expectation I had for you?

16:26.890 --> 16:30.090
Do you think I can still expect it even now? Right?

16:36.990 --> 16:39.590
I'm sorry for stopping you

16:40.990 --> 16:41.690
Let's go

16:43.990 --> 16:46.890
I think Isumi's new shodan match has already started

16:55.590 --> 16:56.390
Kadowaki-san...

17:07.190 --> 17:08.490
Would you like to play me...

17:09.490 --> 17:10.190
Right now?

17:21.190 --> 17:22.490
We'll be using the space for a little bit

17:23.090 --> 17:23.590
Okay

17:29.990 --> 17:31.590
What's wrong, Shindou-Kun?

17:34.690 --> 17:36.090
It looks like it'll be an important game

17:37.790 --> 17:38.390
Why?

17:41.790 --> 17:44.490
Since you can compare me to me from last year

17:45.090 --> 17:47.990
I really want to compare myself to my old self

17:47.990 --> 17:50.790
Clearly... The difference between you and me... Probably isn't much anymore

17:51.490 --> 17:52.790
Don't be surprised when you hear it, but...

17:53.190 --> 17:54.990
My pro exam record is...

17:56.190 --> 17:57.490
You lost to Isumi-san

17:58.190 --> 17:58.890
Isumi...!

17:59.190 --> 18:01.690
That's... I lost to Isumi, but...

18:02.690 --> 18:03.790
Only one loss.

18:05.790 --> 18:08.390
I didn't surrender to Isumi with that one loss

18:08.990 --> 18:11.990
Taking revenge is one of the things I have to do after I become a pro

18:13.590 --> 18:15.590
And the other is...

18:16.090 --> 18:17.290
Playing a game with you

18:17.990 --> 18:20.590
My wish came true rather quickly

18:26.690 --> 18:27.590
Good luck

18:51.490 --> 18:53.590
Hoshi... Hoshi... Hoshi...

18:54.090 --> 18:55.490
Three in a row...

18:58.090 --> 19:00.490
Now... What should I do?

19:02.190 --> 19:03.590
Should I make the first move?

19:04.390 --> 19:05.790
Just like a year and a half ago...?

19:07.190 --> 19:08.990
I was toyed with at that time, but...

19:09.390 --> 19:11.190
That won't happen again to me now

19:14.990 --> 19:17.790
No... I might be wanting to be toyed with...

19:18.890 --> 19:21.090
In the corner of my mind. I feel as though I don't want to lose to anyone, but...

19:21.790 --> 19:24.490
Yearning for a skill which I can't follow...

19:25.190 --> 19:27.690
Is it because I want to see the future this kid is walking on...?

19:29.090 --> 19:32.890
That future...
Which surpasses him greatly...

19:36.790 --> 19:38.790
Is my punch working...?

19:42.290 --> 19:43.590
Or... Are you avoiding...?

19:48.990 --> 19:50.190
Seems like it might be working...

19:55.290 --> 19:58.390
The feeling I get from this Go is different compared to that time...

20:09.690 --> 20:10.690
It's on from now...

20:11.290 --> 20:13.590
He penetrated into my strong territory...

20:55.190 --> 20:56.790
What did you say your name was?

21:04.490 --> 21:05.490
It's Isumi-kun

21:06.190 --> 21:07.290
Isumi Shinichiro

21:08.590 --> 21:09.790
Isumi, eh...

21:10.090 --> 21:11.490
I'll keep that in mind

21:12.290 --> 21:17.490
The new comers these days were unbecoming... But after Touya's son appeared...

21:17.490 --> 21:20.190
Interesting kids are starting to appear... Slowly...

21:28.090 --> 21:31.090
It was worth hanging around in the Go world

21:31.890 --> 21:36.990
Plus... He hasn't shown his true abilities yet...

21:50.690 --> 21:51.890
This kid...

22:03.090 --> 22:03.690
It's no good...

22:04.090 --> 22:04.690
He got me!

22:26.190 --> 22:27.090
I resign

22:28.490 --> 22:29.490
Thank you very much

22:32.390 --> 22:34.190
This move I made here was good

22:34.190 --> 22:36.390
But you came in by putting it together here which prohibited me from doing anything

22:36.990 --> 22:39.190
That move was one I thought of instantly

22:39.890 --> 22:42.390
I thought it would be pretty difficult in the last phase, but...

22:43.090 --> 22:45.990
But your judgement was levelheaded in dealing with it

22:47.390 --> 22:48.690
I did it, but I did it pretty good...

22:49.490 --> 22:51.590
Thank you. It was a good thing I played you

22:53.590 --> 22:55.690
Whan I think that there are Go players like you...

22:56.490 --> 22:58.290
It's worth taking the path of pros

23:06.490 --> 23:08.690
I forgot all about Isumi-san's game!

23:10.690 --> 23:12.490
Kadowaki-san came to watch that too, right?

23:13.290 --> 23:14.690
I wonder if they are still playing...

23:24.090 --> 23:24.890
Kadowaki-san...

23:27.890 --> 23:30.290
You mean Isumi's game?
Let's go... Let's so

23:31.690 --> 23:32.390
Kadowaki-san...

23:33.590 --> 23:37.090
You just said that it was a good thing to play me...

23:38.490 --> 23:39.690
Was that the truth?

23:45.390 --> 23:46.890
It's... The truth

23:47.490 --> 23:48.590
You are strong

23:50.190 --> 23:52.290
What I just said was the truth

23:53.890 --> 23:54.390
Anything else

23:55.390 --> 23:56.990
That's not all, right?

23:59.690 --> 24:00.190
No...

24:00.190 --> 24:02.290
That... That's...

24:03.590 --> 24:07.190
How should I say....?
You, in the former years...

24:08.290 --> 24:12.390
Seemed stronger after all...

24:19.990 --> 24:20.990
I'm sorry...

24:21.590 --> 24:22.590
Don't worry about it

24:24.690 --> 24:26.290
I think so, too

24:41.190 --> 24:42.590
He thinks that way, too?

24:43.590 --> 24:45.690
Former years of himself was stronger...

24:45.990 --> 24:47.990
It's not a situation you can laugh about, kid

24:49.890 --> 24:56.490
I really can't figure out if he is really an incredible player or not

25:01.290 --> 25:01.790
Shindou

25:02.090 --> 25:02.690
Waya

25:03.490 --> 25:04.290
Is it over?

25:04.790 --> 25:05.890
What happened to Isumi-san?

25:06.190 --> 25:08.090
Isumi-san won by 6.5 moku

25:08.390 --> 25:09.390
They just started the examination

25:09.690 --> 25:10.990
6.5 moku?

25:10.990 --> 25:11.790
Wow

25:11.790 --> 25:14.190
Why are you coming now? You're late

25:14.990 --> 25:16.790
I met Kadowaki-san on the way

25:17.190 --> 25:19.390
I played a game on the second floor just now

25:21.890 --> 25:22.790
It's over already?

25:23.590 --> 25:24.190
Kadowaki-san...

25:25.090 --> 25:25.790
What happened?

25:26.190 --> 25:27.490
Isumi-san won...

25:27.990 --> 25:28.890
By 6.5 Moku

25:29.390 --> 25:30.990
umm.. Kadowaki-san...

25:32.290 --> 25:34.390
Do you know Shindou?

25:35.190 --> 25:35.890
Do I know him?

25:36.890 --> 25:40.490
Rather than knowing each other...
I played against him once before.

25:41.290 --> 25:44.890
When he was an Insei about a year and a half ago, I called him over...

25:45.290 --> 25:47.490
I lost completely at that time

25:48.190 --> 25:51.190
The kid we were talking about earlier was really Shindou after all!

25:51.590 --> 25:53.790
But I played him again today...

25:54.990 --> 25:58.290
I felt as though he was stronger before...

25:59.790 --> 26:02.790
Plus... He said he also thinks so too and just laughed

26:03.390 --> 26:04.890
I just can't figure him out

26:06.690 --> 26:09.490
I don't know either.
It's confusing

26:10.190 --> 26:11.390
I told you...

26:11.790 --> 26:13.590
It's no use worrying about Shindou

26:14.190 --> 26:14.690
That's right.

26:15.190 --> 26:16.790
Let's worry about ourselves

26:17.290 --> 26:20.790
We weren't the only ones who were moving towards Hokutohai

26:21.790 --> 26:26.490
At that time, I didn't know anything about the player candidate from Kansai Go Institute

26:37.090 --> 26:37.690
It's Honda

26:40.390 --> 26:40.990
Excuse me

26:41.790 --> 26:42.690
You're here

26:43.390 --> 26:45.290
This is Yoshikawa from Kansai Go Institute. He is hachidan

26:45.690 --> 26:47.690
It's been along time since he has been here

26:48.390 --> 26:49.090
Hello

26:54.890 --> 26:55.490
Toshinori

26:55.990 --> 26:58.290
This is Yashiiro Kiyoharu-kun. Who became a pro at the Kansai Go Institute

26:58.290 --> 26:59.690
This is Yashiro Kiyoharu-kun

27:00.090 --> 27:01.790
He is three years younger than you

27:02.390 --> 27:08.390
I remember that sensei had a student who passed the pro exam at the Japan Go Institute...

27:08.890 --> 27:10.690
When I remembered that... I brought him here

27:10.690 --> 27:11.890
He's pretty good

27:11.890 --> 27:12.990
Would you like to play him once?

27:13.690 --> 27:14.190
Yes

27:23.490 --> 27:25.790
Now that I think about it, Ochi said...

27:26.290 --> 27:28.590
That there is an up-and-coming player from Kansai Go Institute...

27:29.090 --> 27:30.290
It must be him

27:31.890 --> 27:34.190
This is like the Hokutohai preliminaries pre-match

27:35.090 --> 27:35.990
I don't want to lose...

27:36.390 --> 27:38.190
Please, do me the honor of teaching me

27:38.190 --> 27:39.290
Good luck

27:56.890 --> 27:58.790
Should I... Try that?

27:59.890 --> 28:00.390
That?

28:20.490 --> 28:21.990
First move. Tengen...

28:32.190 --> 28:32.590
Alright

28:33.390 --> 28:35.290
I'll accept any kind of moves

28:40.890 --> 28:42.590
Yashiro-kun is incredible

28:43.190 --> 28:45.390
Toshinori still has alot to learn

28:45.990 --> 28:48.990
No, Kiyoharu won this time, but...

28:48.990 --> 28:50.690
This is the beginning for Honda-kun aswell

28:50.990 --> 28:53.090
Excuse me for staying so late

29:02.290 --> 29:03.490
First move, Tengen...

29:03.490 --> 29:06.790
Isn't a move which is not used at all in the pro matches, but

29:07.190 --> 29:09.990
That's right, but it becomes a difficult Go

29:10.290 --> 29:12.190
Normally, they'll first play your corner...

29:12.190 --> 29:13.890
It's easy to make a territory in the corners...

29:15.490 --> 29:18.390
But in the middle of the board, Tengen has nothing to do with territory...

29:18.690 --> 29:20.490
Except it keeps the eyes on the entire Go board

29:20.990 --> 29:23.190
If this stone plays its role,. it's victory

29:23.190 --> 29:24.690
If it doesn't, it's defeat

29:25.490 --> 29:27.890
The opponent will play as it Confuses you

29:28.490 --> 29:30.090
Thoughts are simple...

29:32.190 --> 29:33.990
But the method of playing is difficult

29:34.690 --> 29:36.590
However, first move Tengen

29:36.590 --> 29:38.290
Which was used by the kid from Kansai
He played its role properly.

29:38.590 --> 29:39.770
It's Honda's complete defeat

29:39.990 --> 29:41.270
He said he was fifteen?

29:41.290 --> 29:42.330
He's incredible

29:42.690 --> 29:45.190
Did he say he was going to enter the preliminaries for the Hokutohai?

29:46.290 --> 29:49.290
Now that I think about it, did you say the preliminary schedule notice came?

29:53.190 --> 29:53.790
Toshinori

29:54.690 --> 29:55.390
Yes

29:55.790 --> 29:58.190
Hokutohai's preliminary schedule... What happened?

29:58.890 --> 30:01.990
Four players from Tokyo and four from Middle Kansai...

30:02.590 --> 30:04.790
A total of eight players will play in April

30:05.290 --> 30:07.890
Tokyo will host the first preliminary which will select four players

30:08.590 --> 30:09.690
That's next week...

30:10.890 --> 30:11.990
Next week...

30:12.690 --> 30:15.790
All the ones who joined recently are strong...

30:16.490 --> 30:18.290
You must do your best, too

30:18.890 --> 30:23.590
That's right... I still have a lot to learn even if I compare myself to Ochi

30:25.790 --> 30:26.490
Toshinori

30:34.190 --> 30:34.790
Yes

30:37.190 --> 30:40.290
Hokutohai
Tokyo District First Round of Preliminaries

30:46.790 --> 30:48.090
Let me tell you one thing

30:49.290 --> 30:50.690
The road to becoming a pro is long...

30:51.590 --> 30:53.490
Long and there isn't any resting along the way...

30:54.890 --> 30:56.190
You must study it for life

30:58.590 --> 31:00.090
Do you understand, Toshinori?

31:04.190 --> 31:06.890
That's right. I'm a Pro Go player

31:08.590 --> 31:09.890
The road to becoming a pro is long...

31:10.590 --> 31:12.390
Long and there isn't any resting in the Go world...

31:14.790 --> 31:16.190
I must study it for life

31:22.790 --> 31:23.890
First move, Tengen...

31:24.990 --> 31:27.090
It's an iteresting move you played, Honda-san

31:27.690 --> 31:28.290
Alright

31:54.890 --> 31:55.490
How about it?

31:55.790 --> 31:58.190
You can't easily connect the black in this case, right?

31:59.490 --> 32:01.490
I'll make that first move Tengen into a bad move

32:04.490 --> 32:05.190
In order to do that,

32:05.690 --> 32:06.990
I can't fall back here!

32:10.790 --> 32:12.290
A world which I'll be in forever!

32:14.290 --> 32:18.290
Honda-san, that kind of play...
You can't beat me with that!

32:26.990 --> 32:27.690
I resign

32:32.090 --> 32:32.790
I lost

32:40.890 --> 32:41.690
I resign!

32:43.090 --> 32:45.090
Hokutohai's first preliminary is over

32:45.790 --> 32:46.890
Next preliminary is in two months from now

32:48.090 --> 32:49.290
I'll definitely become a memeber!

32:50.490 --> 32:52.490
Touya, by that time...

32:52.990 --> 32:55.790
I will be a member of Japans team just like you are!

33:36.190 --> 33:36.890
Hikaru

33:37.890 --> 33:38.690
I'm coming now

33:41.490 --> 33:42.390
See you later

33:48.590 --> 33:49.690
Hikaru, what are you doing?

33:50.090 --> 33:51.190
Let's play one game

33:53.690 --> 33:55.690
Were you looking in the shed again?

33:57.390 --> 33:59.890
You always go in there when you come here

34:00.590 --> 34:03.590
If you want that Go board, I'll give it to you

34:04.990 --> 34:07.490
What? You said I couldn't have it before

34:09.190 --> 34:11.690
It's different now, since you became a pro

34:13.090 --> 34:13.690
Do you want it?

34:15.290 --> 34:17.590
No, I have the one Grandpa bought me...

34:18.190 --> 34:20.090
So just leave that Go board there

34:20.690 --> 34:21.290
Alright

34:21.690 --> 34:22.790
now...
Let's play

34:25.390 --> 34:26.290
Now, Nigiri...

34:26.890 --> 34:29.890
Grandpa, do you understand that I'm a pro?

34:30.190 --> 34:31.490
Why don't you place afew stones on the board?

34:31.490 --> 34:32.390
Don't be silly

34:32.690 --> 34:34.690
You think you can beat me easily

34:35.790 --> 34:36.790
I'm black

34:38.490 --> 34:38.990
Oh yeah

34:39.490 --> 34:41.790
Don't you have a game with kudan this week?

34:43.690 --> 34:44.390
This is it... this

34:44.790 --> 34:47.590
Honinbou match, second preliminary...
Second round!

34:47.990 --> 34:50.890
Morishita Shigeo kudan verses Shindou Hikaru shodan

34:53.390 --> 34:58.190
Every week, I study at the strategy sessions lead by that Morishita-sensei

34:58.990 --> 34:59.990
It's already been two years

35:00.590 --> 35:02.790
I've been studying there since I was an Insei...

35:04.890 --> 35:06.390
That kind of person is your opponent?

35:07.090 --> 35:10.690
That might be a difficult match for you

35:11.590 --> 35:12.390
It might be difficult

35:12.790 --> 35:15.390
But in order to move up...
I must defeat any kind of opponent

35:16.990 --> 35:17.690
Good luck

35:18.290 --> 35:19.690
Is that right? Do your best

35:20.390 --> 35:21.490
Good luck

35:21.890 --> 35:25.590
Alright, first... I'm going to beat grandpa by 50 moku!

35:25.590 --> 35:28.490
W-what? You! You almost gave me a heart attack!

35:42.090 --> 35:42.990
Good morning

36:06.290 --> 36:06.990
Morning

36:14.390 --> 36:17.190
Honinbou Match league

36:28.490 --> 36:31.290
Well, I thought this day would come someday, but...

36:32.490 --> 36:33.690
Since it came like this...

36:36.290 --> 36:38.290
It seems it came too early... Or.. Perhaps too late...

36:53.090 --> 36:54.890
He's an opponent that I can see through completely, but...

36:57.290 --> 36:58.290
Good morning

36:58.790 --> 36:59.590
Ogata-san

37:00.690 --> 37:01.390
Morning

37:04.790 --> 37:06.990
This is his first game in a pro league

37:08.390 --> 37:17.190
Honinbou League Fifth Match
Ogata Seiji · Jyuudan Master
Vs
Touya Akira · Sandan

37:24.290 --> 37:32.990
Honinbou League Second Preliminary Second Round
Morishita Sigeo · Kudan
Vs
Shindou Hikaru · Shodan

37:40.090 --> 37:42.890
This kid is confident right now

37:44.390 --> 37:47.890
I must gather my strength if I want to attack

38:02.790 --> 38:05.190
He has good judgement, plus... He's fast

38:06.590 --> 38:08.690
I played him in the strategy sessions

38:09.490 --> 38:11.890
But I can't see the bottom of his talent

38:13.690 --> 38:17.090
But he has only played against me in the strategy sessions

38:17.890 --> 38:20.390
He doesn't know me in the place of a match

38:21.390 --> 38:22.390
I have the upper hand

38:23.290 --> 38:24.790
I just have to go along like this

38:26.290 --> 38:27.990
If sensei attacks the bottom side...

38:28.390 --> 38:31.590
I will pressure him by winning the upper territories

38:38.390 --> 38:40.490
When Ogata-san became the student of my father was...

38:41.290 --> 38:42.590
Before I was even born

38:43.490 --> 38:44.590
Excluding my father

38:44.990 --> 38:47.190
I played against Ogata-san the most

38:48.490 --> 38:50.190
I can do it. This game...

38:50.990 --> 38:51.890
I have a good feeling

38:52.690 --> 38:53.290
I have the confidence

38:54.390 --> 38:58.190
It's the confidence I've gotten from the games I played against Ogata-san during the strategy sessions

39:07.890 --> 39:09.190
No...

39:10.590 --> 39:11.690
If this place opens up...!

39:18.890 --> 39:19.590
Be patient...

39:20.090 --> 39:22.290
If I fall back here, I'll ruin this Go!

39:41.190 --> 39:43.190
Somehow... He seems different than usual...

39:47.490 --> 39:48.590
I'm being pressured by the mood...

40:03.990 --> 40:06.990
My fingers aren't coming off the stones that easily...

40:08.690 --> 40:09.490
Damn it...

40:09.890 --> 40:10.990
I can't get nervous...!

40:11.590 --> 40:12.490
I can't fall back...!

40:19.390 --> 40:20.590
He took his hand off...?!

40:24.290 --> 40:25.190
He... Got me.

40:25.490 --> 40:26.790
The center was first...

40:37.390 --> 40:38.290
An advancement such as this...!

40:47.990 --> 40:50.790
I must bring back the lead somehow...

40:54.690 --> 40:55.290
It's a big problem.

40:55.890 --> 40:57.690
It's over if the form scatters...

41:21.090 --> 41:21.790
I lost

41:31.790 --> 41:32.490
I resign...!

41:38.690 --> 41:40.590
Let's review it in another room

41:41.590 --> 41:43.590
Touya-Kun, you fought well

41:43.590 --> 41:47.090
But I'm sure it was a bit difficult since he is a close senpai of yours

41:47.990 --> 41:48.690
I...

41:49.090 --> 41:51.390
It's natural that you would be nervous, too

41:52.190 --> 41:54.390
The reason for defeat is that after all, right?

41:55.390 --> 41:57.390
He was not nervous

41:59.190 --> 42:01.090
He wasn't overpowered by me

42:01.590 --> 42:04.490
He wasn't unreasonable nor was he bluffing

42:05.590 --> 42:08.490
He showed his skills calmly as he always does

42:08.990 --> 42:12.990
So you're saying that he splendidly played his game no matter who the opponent was?

42:13.490 --> 42:15.190
He's incredible for a fifteen year old

42:15.890 --> 42:17.590
I'm not praising him

42:19.490 --> 42:22.090
You can say that the difference in skills have been displayed

42:22.790 --> 42:25.190
Since there weren't any minus elements

42:28.690 --> 42:29.690
Ogata-sensei...

42:30.790 --> 42:32.390
You were trying to beat me, but...

42:33.190 --> 42:34.990
You definitely realized it through this match, right?

42:38.990 --> 42:40.490
You are below me!

42:41.390 --> 42:42.290
Ogata-sensei...

42:43.490 --> 42:45.290
I can't find any room to spare in his appearance...

42:46.490 --> 42:48.190
“You're below me”...

42:48.590 --> 42:49.990
He couldn't stand it without saying those words...

42:51.090 --> 42:53.790
That's how close Touya-Kun has pursued him

42:54.790 --> 42:56.590
Ogata Jyuudan, Go master!

42:58.590 --> 43:02.990
I've been watching you for two years in the strategy sessions which are held once a week...

43:04.390 --> 43:05.390
You've grown

43:09.090 --> 43:10.790
I thought that I've grown...

43:13.290 --> 43:17.990
I never felt dispirited even when I played sensei in the strategy sessions

43:19.290 --> 43:20.490
That's how I thought...

43:21.290 --> 43:21.790
But...

43:22.290 --> 43:24.690
I couldn't surpass sensei in the place of a match

43:26.390 --> 43:28.390
There's something I lack still

43:29.390 --> 43:32.440
Place of a match.. Is it?

43:32.490 --> 43:36.890
You'll never know the fear of a Go player.
Unless you fight them in the place of a match

43:39.290 --> 43:40.490
But that fan...

43:41.590 --> 43:44.690
You didn't start carrying it around for looks, did you?

43:45.990 --> 43:49.390
It's to show some kind of determination, right?

43:50.390 --> 43:52.390
That you must attack...

44:36.190 --> 44:37.190
There she is. There she is

44:37.190 --> 44:37.990
Kaneko-san!

44:40.590 --> 44:41.990
Kaneko-san, where's Mitani-kun?

44:42.490 --> 44:45.490
He already went home. Why?

44:46.190 --> 44:48.290
We want to take a group picture of the Go club

44:48.790 --> 44:50.290
Shindou-Kun isn't here, either...

44:50.290 --> 44:51.990
That's enough about Hikaru!

44:52.390 --> 44:53.990
He quit during the first year of Jr.High

44:55.990 --> 44:57.790
Nori-chan, will you take our picture?

44:58.790 --> 44:59.390
Sure

45:00.490 --> 45:01.390
Now, cheeeesse!

45:03.090 --> 45:03.790
Thank you

45:04.290 --> 45:04.790
Akari

45:06.390 --> 45:07.790
Hikaru, what?

45:08.390 --> 45:11.790
My mom and your mom are chatting away over there

45:13.090 --> 45:15.190
I want to hurry up and eat...

45:15.590 --> 45:18.190
We've been friends since we were very young...

45:18.790 --> 45:20.490
They probably have alot to talk about

45:21.590 --> 45:23.390
Should we retake the picture with Shindou-Kun in it?

45:24.190 --> 45:24.990
Let me see that for a minute

45:31.090 --> 45:32.690
Which high school are you going to?

45:33.190 --> 45:34.890
I didn't take the public school exam, yet

45:36.290 --> 45:37.790
You're still a student in preparation to take the exam

45:38.390 --> 45:40.790
But... No matter where I go

45:40.790 --> 45:41.890
I'm going to join the Go club

45:42.190 --> 45:43.690
It would be nice if they have a Go club

45:44.190 --> 45:45.490
If they don't have it, I'll make one!

45:48.190 --> 45:49.690
Just as Tsutsui-san did...

45:50.390 --> 45:51.890
Just as hard as Koike tried...

45:52.490 --> 45:53.790
I'm going to try it, too!

45:55.290 --> 45:56.290
Yeah, do your best

45:57.690 --> 45:58.890
At that time, Hikaru...

45:59.590 --> 46:01.890
Will you come and teach once in awhile?

46:03.190 --> 46:03.990
You can't?

46:03.990 --> 46:05.990
Do I have to pay for pros?

46:06.490 --> 46:08.690
I don't need money.
I'll come so don't worry

46:09.090 --> 46:09.790
Really?

46:11.490 --> 46:13.490
Of course. Any days I don't have a game...

46:17.190 --> 46:17.890
And...

46:18.390 --> 46:20.490
Hokutohai's second preliminary has started

46:23.590 --> 46:24.890
Waya, hello

46:25.790 --> 46:26.490
Shindou

46:27.590 --> 46:29.290
It's finally the Hokutohai

46:29.290 --> 46:29.390
Yeah... Finally
It's finally the Hokutohai

46:29.390 --> 46:31.090
Yeah... Finally

46:32.190 --> 46:33.690
Two players from the Kansai Go Institute

46:34.190 --> 46:35.490
One player from Central headquarters

46:36.190 --> 46:37.490
One player from Kansai headquarters

46:38.390 --> 46:40.390
Me, Waya, Ochi, and Ingaki-san...

46:40.890 --> 46:43.490
Four players from Tokyo are all seperated

46:44.390 --> 46:46.890
Well, since we won't be playing each other...

46:47.490 --> 46:49.890
Let's comfortably eat lunch together

47:05.390 --> 47:06.890
Shindou and I won't play each other...

47:07.790 --> 47:09.290
Truthfully, I'm thankful

47:11.690 --> 47:15.190
At Morishita-sensei's strategy sessions or strategy sessions at my apartment...

47:15.590 --> 47:18.390
There were times where I couldn't follow his deep thoughts

47:20.490 --> 47:21.990
Because he is always near me

47:22.490 --> 47:25.390
I feel the difference in our skills whether I want to or not

47:26.490 --> 47:29.590
Hokutohai
Player Selection Match - First Round

47:29.590 --> 47:31.590
Then I'll confirm the rules
Hokutohai
Player Selection Match - First Round

47:32.990 --> 47:35.290
Match time is one hour and a half per player

47:35.890 --> 47:37.490
After you use up all of your time,

47:37.490 --> 47:38.590
You have one minute per move

47:39.190 --> 47:40.490
Komi is 5.5

47:40.990 --> 47:43.890
Second round will start here at 3 P.M

47:44.890 --> 47:49.390
The four players who've won in the first round should finish their lunch before that time

47:50.790 --> 47:52.590
Then, please start

47:56.290 --> 47:57.190
Good luck

48:30.590 --> 48:31.390
Shitatsuke...?

48:33.190 --> 48:34.590
It's a surprising move...

48:36.090 --> 48:37.990
Is that possible?

48:52.790 --> 48:54.990
It's his choice to use the time limit however he wants to, but...

48:55.490 --> 48:57.490
He already used up twenty minutes on this one move...

49:14.990 --> 49:17.690
After thinking for that long... He played a pretty common move

49:29.190 --> 49:29.890
I lost

49:30.890 --> 49:31.990
Thanks for the game

49:35.390 --> 49:36.690
I lost completely in reading the moves

49:37.590 --> 49:39.590
To someone who was just an Insei not too long ago...

49:44.190 --> 49:47.590
My next opponent will be one of those two...

50:00.290 --> 50:01.990
He completely broke through the middle...!?

50:03.790 --> 50:05.990
I can't believe the white was pressured this much...

50:06.690 --> 50:07.590
Plus... With just a glance

50:07.590 --> 50:09.490
He quickly obtained such an advantageous territory!

50:16.190 --> 50:18.190
This kid... Is strong

50:23.490 --> 50:25.090
Now, next is the second round

50:26.490 --> 50:29.690
If we win this time, we become the reps of Hokutohai's Japan team

50:33.390 --> 50:35.290
My second round opponent is Ochi

50:35.890 --> 50:37.790
Since the number of participants are small...

50:37.790 --> 50:39.990
You will play against your friends, too

50:41.090 --> 50:42.590
Ochi definitely plays well

50:43.190 --> 50:46.590
But I've always done well against him even from the Insei years

50:47.390 --> 50:48.090
You did

50:49.890 --> 50:50.890
I want to win!

50:52.790 --> 50:55.590
My opponent is Yashiro after all

50:56.190 --> 50:57.590
The one Honda-san mentioned?

50:58.790 --> 51:00.090
The one who played Tengen for his first move

51:01.390 --> 51:04.690
I know that he's pretty strong because Honda-san told me, but...

51:05.990 --> 51:07.190
I wanted to play against him once

51:08.390 --> 51:09.190
I'm really looking forward to it

51:13.790 --> 51:14.590
Yashiro-kun...

51:15.290 --> 51:17.590
I'm not playing against Yashiro nor Hikaru...

51:19.290 --> 51:19.890
It's fortunate

51:21.690 --> 51:23.990
I don't care how they fight it out...

51:30.290 --> 51:31.390
I'm pissed off...

51:31.790 --> 51:34.090
I didn't get to display my skills from ordinary times

51:34.590 --> 51:35.090
Yashiro,

51:35.690 --> 51:37.590
I lost in the first round, but...

51:37.890 --> 51:39.190
You should do well

51:39.590 --> 51:42.490
What an embarrasment it would be, if both of us from Kansai Go Institute lose

51:42.990 --> 51:45.290
What kind of player is Shindou?

51:45.890 --> 51:47.090
You saw my game

51:51.790 --> 51:53.390
It doesn't matter who the opponent is

51:54.790 --> 51:58.490
I don't care what happens to Kansai Go Institute, but...

51:59.790 --> 52:01.990
In order to become a rep of Japans team

52:02.790 --> 52:04.890
I can't lose to anyone

52:05.590 --> 52:06.390
That's it

52:07.290 --> 52:10.790
Hokutohai
Player Selection Match - Second Round

52:10.790 --> 52:12.090
Then, everyone take a seat
Hokutohai
Player Selection Match - Second Round

52:12.090 --> 52:12.490
Then, everyone take a seat

52:13.890 --> 52:15.690
That side is Waya-kun and Ochi-kun

52:16.590 --> 52:18.690
This side is Shindou-Kun and Yashiro-kun

52:29.090 --> 52:30.990
This games two winners will be selected as the players

52:31.490 --> 52:34.990
Who will represent Japans team in Hokutohai.
Which is to be held a month from now

52:41.990 --> 52:43.790
Then, Please start

52:50.090 --> 52:51.390
Yashiro is black

52:53.190 --> 52:54.590
What would he play...?

52:56.390 --> 52:57.590
First move, Tengen...

52:59.690 --> 53:01.490
I played a game at the sensei's place..

53:02.290 --> 53:05.790
At that time, he played Tengen as his first move and I lost

53:06.490 --> 53:10.890
I got pissed off so I found a Kifu of a pro who played Tengen as the first move...

53:11.690 --> 53:15.690
And I was black today so I played it against you, Shindou, but...

53:17.090 --> 53:18.190
I lost again

53:22.190 --> 53:24.290
That Go was really making my heart beat, Honda-san

53:26.790 --> 53:27.490
Good luck

53:45.090 --> 53:45.890
First move Tengen...

53:46.990 --> 53:48.690
Is he not going to play that against me...?

53:51.390 --> 53:53.090
Play it... Hey!

54:12.890 --> 54:13.890
5-5?

54:33.990 --> 54:35.590
I can't belive that he played 5-5 on his first move!

54:36.690 --> 54:39.890
That is not a move you can make unless he has considerable confidence in his skills

54:41.890 --> 54:43.190
That's just like Yashiro, but...

54:43.590 --> 54:45.490
Why at a time like this...?

54:45.890 --> 54:46.890
First move... 5-5...

54:47.690 --> 54:49.190
It's not a move players don't play at all, but...

54:50.090 --> 54:53.990
It's probably a move they don't even play as much as the first move, Tengen

55:06.390 --> 55:07.490
Not bad!

55:29.590 --> 55:30.990
Second move... Tengen!!

55:54.190 --> 55:55.990
No, it's not bad

55:56.890 --> 56:00.090
If my move was aiming for a confusing fight...

56:01.290 --> 56:05.890
He plays the Tengen which controls the whole board. He's not bad

56:06.790 --> 56:08.890
Second move... Tengen

56:09.990 --> 56:10.790
It's surprising

56:12.190 --> 56:13.690
Second move... Tengen...

56:15.290 --> 56:16.990
What kind of person is he...?

56:17.490 --> 56:19.690
More incredible than Yashiro...

56:33.390 --> 56:34.590
W-what...

56:35.390 --> 56:38.090
Third move... 5-5 again??

56:43.790 --> 56:45.490
What are those two doing...?

56:46.690 --> 56:47.890
This guy...

56:51.390 --> 56:53.890
If you play it like that... I can't lose, either

56:59.190 --> 57:01.690
I really want to overturn the board...

57:02.190 --> 57:04.590
Yashiro, do you have the confidence to beat him, right?

57:12.890 --> 57:13.890
Each at Hoshi

57:14.390 --> 57:15.590
Kakari...

57:16.090 --> 57:16.690
And...

57:18.790 --> 57:20.490
I'll completely seal the Tengen!

57:27.190 --> 57:28.090
Do you think I'll let you do that?!

57:28.990 --> 57:30.090
Why don't you try!

57:46.090 --> 57:47.790
Shifting of black... It's a good move

57:50.890 --> 57:51.770
He came to break through!

58:01.390 --> 58:02.990
Now, how will you respond?

58:19.190 --> 58:21.190
It's shape I've built with hard work...

58:21.690 --> 58:22.890
How will you respond, Ochi?

58:37.990 --> 58:39.690
It changed into positive Kakari...

58:40.290 --> 58:42.490
It might be difficult for Ochi...

58:54.590 --> 58:57.990
White territory is big, but there's only one...

58:58.590 --> 58:59.890
Waya, looks good...

59:01.290 --> 59:05.090
In the beginning, Ochi's offensive movement aimed for the main spot aswell, but...

59:07.290 --> 59:08.990
No one is next to this game?

59:09.890 --> 59:11.790
Did everyone go to another room?

59:19.990 --> 59:21.490
What... Is this?!

59:22.090 --> 59:24.890
This corner, that corner...
I can't tell the order of the moves...

59:25.290 --> 59:27.390
Plus... They crossed each other at Tengen...!

59:29.090 --> 59:30.390
What is this?

59:54.690 --> 59:55.090
How is it?

59:55.490 --> 59:57.790
Wow, it's really an incredible battle

59:59.890 --> 1:00:03.490
When one penetrates the other's weakness, instead of accepting it... They counterattack...

1:00:06.590 --> 1:00:07.390
It's a big confussion...

1:00:08.190 --> 1:00:10.090
Here and there are all thined ground

1:00:10.490 --> 1:00:12.690
Jeez... How can they play such frightening Go as this...?

1:00:13.190 --> 1:00:14.990
This move that the white has made is a good move, right?

1:00:16.590 --> 1:00:18.390
That's right, he connects his own stones...

1:00:18.990 --> 1:00:23.790
At the same time, he cuts through the opponent's stones while he invades towards the top

1:00:24.790 --> 1:00:26.790
But Yashiro isn't falling back either

1:00:27.490 --> 1:00:30.290
Truthfully, I never thought he could play at this level

1:00:31.790 --> 1:00:35.290
It's regrettable...
That one of the two has to fall...

1:00:37.090 --> 1:00:42.090
If it's these two, they could put up an interesting match with Korea and China

1:00:45.790 --> 1:00:47.490
Shindou, Yashiro...

1:00:48.190 --> 1:00:51.590
These two and... If Touya Akira is added...

1:00:55.190 --> 1:00:55.790
Touya...

1:00:57.490 --> 1:00:58.190
Kurata-san

1:00:58.690 --> 1:01:00.090
You came to watch it, too?

1:01:00.590 --> 1:01:02.590
Hokutohai representative selection preliminary

1:01:03.390 --> 1:01:04.590
Kurata-san, too?

1:01:04.590 --> 1:01:07.590
I am Japan's team leader!

1:01:08.190 --> 1:01:08.990
Kurata-san is?

1:01:09.490 --> 1:01:12.690
Yeah, I couldn't just sit around when Korea and China are the opponents

1:01:13.390 --> 1:01:13.990
Let's go

1:01:16.990 --> 1:01:18.490
One of the two other members...

1:01:19.390 --> 1:01:22.890
Shindou, it's you... Right?

1:01:35.690 --> 1:01:37.090
It's here. He played here!

1:01:40.490 --> 1:01:42.990
It's a move that defends as it closes in

1:01:42.990 --> 1:01:43.190
Wow

1:01:43.190 --> 1:01:43.690
It's incredible...

1:01:43.690 --> 1:01:45.390
It's one move that's completely solid

1:01:48.190 --> 1:01:48.790
But

1:01:49.290 --> 1:01:51.790
this Shindou-Yashiro's game was really incredible

1:01:53.790 --> 1:01:55.690
Even though the match has been decided with this one move...

1:01:56.190 --> 1:01:57.390
But still... It's a bit regrettable

1:01:58.790 --> 1:02:01.790
It's regrettable for this kid... He plays this well...

1:02:09.790 --> 1:02:10.390
Impossible...!

1:02:14.990 --> 1:02:15.590
Shindou!

1:02:42.090 --> 1:02:44.490
The one who is winning is white... Shindou!

1:02:46.090 --> 1:02:48.590
But... What kind of Go is this...?

1:02:49.190 --> 1:02:50.290
I can't see the order of the moves...

1:02:50.790 --> 1:02:52.890
What kind of Go... Was this?

1:03:04.990 --> 1:03:05.490
Touya!

1:03:12.690 --> 1:03:15.090
All you can see in your eyes is Shindou's game?

1:03:16.190 --> 1:03:17.290
It's as always

1:03:26.490 --> 1:03:31.990
I admit that Waya played well, but if the stones on this side die... It's over

1:03:45.790 --> 1:03:46.590
I resign

1:03:47.590 --> 1:03:48.790
Thank you very much

1:03:53.790 --> 1:03:58.590
Touya, with this... I am a Hokutohai player who stands shoulder to shoulder with you

1:04:00.990 --> 1:04:04.890
Between Waya and me... The answer to who is better suited as a player has been answered

1:04:05.590 --> 1:04:06.690
It was me after all

1:04:10.290 --> 1:04:11.690
Damm it!

1:04:14.290 --> 1:04:15.790
Let's not worry about it, it's over

1:04:16.290 --> 1:04:17.390
I should just go home

1:04:20.190 --> 1:04:20.890
Ochi...

1:04:28.990 --> 1:04:30.490
What... Is this game?!

1:04:33.990 --> 1:04:35.290
First move 5-5...?

1:04:36.190 --> 1:04:37.390
Second move, Tengen!?

1:04:37.890 --> 1:04:40.690
And! On the third move, Yashiro played 5-5 again!

1:04:42.090 --> 1:04:43.990
It's really an incredible game

1:04:47.290 --> 1:04:49.790
Black has covered it well like this, but...

1:04:50.490 --> 1:04:53.990
It was incredible for white to attack from there alone...

1:04:54.390 --> 1:04:57.890
After Shindou broke through, his fight was something to see

1:05:00.090 --> 1:05:02.690
Black is frozen by the sight of white

1:05:03.290 --> 1:05:05.290
But Yashiro didn't just sit and watch

1:05:11.390 --> 1:05:12.490
Target move on that side...!

1:05:13.390 --> 1:05:13.690
right

1:05:14.290 --> 1:05:19.690
he left the extremely uncertain upper portion alone and tried to win this side

1:05:24.990 --> 1:05:28.590
Of course, that was blocked by Shindou aswell...

1:05:35.790 --> 1:05:38.690
The match is almost over, since he allowed the white to make an important move...

1:05:39.090 --> 1:05:41.490
They both have the skills which are regretful to fail

1:05:43.890 --> 1:05:47.690
Ochi-kun, you're a represesntative player. Congratulations

1:05:51.090 --> 1:05:52.690
I'm going to see the game

1:05:58.090 --> 1:06:00.490
That Ochi has been decided?

1:06:00.490 --> 1:06:00.990
Yes

1:06:01.590 --> 1:06:03.290
How was Ochi's game?

1:06:03.690 --> 1:06:05.090
Level was high

1:06:05.890 --> 1:06:08.790
But compared to this Shindou-Yashiro match...

1:06:09.590 --> 1:06:12.290
Ochi-kun and Waya-kun know each other well...

1:06:12.690 --> 1:06:15.090
And that could've helped the other opponent...

1:06:15.590 --> 1:06:18.290
This game is just too incredible after all

1:06:19.990 --> 1:06:22.290
Yashiro, huh? It's regrettable, but...

1:06:23.190 --> 1:06:26.490
There's nothing we can do if the result of the preliminary is like this

1:06:27.390 --> 1:06:29.390
No matter who looks at it, they can tell...

1:06:29.890 --> 1:06:32.290
The difference between Ochi and Yashiro's Go sense...

1:06:33.690 --> 1:06:35.790
Shall we go and watch the match for a little while?

1:06:40.490 --> 1:06:41.490
Watanabe-sensei...

1:06:42.190 --> 1:06:43.690
Have the players been decided?

1:06:44.490 --> 1:06:45.290
Kosemura-san

1:06:47.290 --> 1:06:51.390
This is Hokuto communication system's Togari-san and Aikawa-san

1:06:51.990 --> 1:06:52.790
I'm Togari

1:06:53.290 --> 1:06:54.090
I'm Aikawa

1:06:54.590 --> 1:06:56.490
We just stopped by

1:06:57.190 --> 1:06:58.990
How are the games going?

1:06:59.790 --> 1:07:01.790
One person has been selected, Ochi

1:07:02.290 --> 1:07:04.490
We'll know the other person after the game is over, but...

1:07:05.190 --> 1:07:05.990
Watanabe-sensei

1:07:06.690 --> 1:07:07.890
Yashiro threw in the stones

1:07:09.190 --> 1:07:10.290
Is that right? I'll be there now

1:07:10.890 --> 1:07:12.590
Yashiro must've lost, right?

1:07:13.290 --> 1:07:15.190
Looks like it. Then...

1:07:16.890 --> 1:07:17.790
Let us go, too

1:07:18.190 --> 1:07:20.590
No, we'll wait here

1:07:21.090 --> 1:07:21.890
Is that what you want?

1:07:22.390 --> 1:07:25.390
Then, since I have to go get their pictures and comments...

1:07:26.290 --> 1:07:27.290
Please take care of it

1:07:32.190 --> 1:07:34.990
Congratulations for being selected as a Hokutohai member!

1:07:49.690 --> 1:07:51.290
But, Ochi-kun

1:07:52.690 --> 1:07:55.790
Please...
Let me have a match with Yashiro

1:07:56.490 --> 1:07:59.290
I would like for you to decide on the member from the result of that!

1:08:01.090 --> 1:08:04.390
Everyone would complain if I became a member like this, right?

1:08:05.090 --> 1:08:06.690
By seeing their game...

1:08:06.990 --> 1:08:10.490
I can't accept the fact that I was selected!

1:08:11.090 --> 1:08:15.690
I want to confirm who deserves to be a member between Yashiro and I!

1:08:21.190 --> 1:08:23.290
Ochi... That's incredible pride...

1:08:23.690 --> 1:08:27.690
I was happy that I wasn't paired up with Shindou or ashiro...

1:08:33.190 --> 1:08:37.190
The kid, from Kansai Go Institute that Superior was talking about, lost

1:08:38.190 --> 1:08:42.690
Yeah, I guess he wasn't as good as the person in Kansai Go Institute said he was

1:08:43.890 --> 1:08:47.390
But you never know if the opponent was the one with incredible skills

1:08:49.090 --> 1:08:50.390
I hope that's the case

1:08:51.390 --> 1:08:52.990
It's not that Japan must win, but...

1:08:53.390 --> 1:08:55.090
It'll be difficult if the quality drops in the compitition

1:08:55.390 --> 1:08:57.390
Since the competition must be popular...

1:08:58.090 --> 1:08:59.390
Superior...

1:08:59.390 --> 1:09:00.290
Togari-san...!

1:09:04.490 --> 1:09:05.790
Are you done with the data gathering?

1:09:06.390 --> 1:09:07.990
No, truthfully...

1:09:10.790 --> 1:09:12.090
I heard the story

1:09:13.290 --> 1:09:15.390
I heard you want to add another game to the preliminary matches?

1:09:16.090 --> 1:09:16.690
Yes

1:09:17.290 --> 1:09:18.690
I know it's a difficult request, but...

1:09:20.490 --> 1:09:21.190
Alright.

1:09:21.790 --> 1:09:22.290
You may do so

1:09:23.490 --> 1:09:26.190
But we have a situation on this side too

1:09:26.690 --> 1:09:28.290
so if you can rush it...

1:09:28.590 --> 1:09:30.590
I don't care if I have to it tromorrow...

1:09:31.490 --> 1:09:32.490
How about it Yashiro?

1:09:32.790 --> 1:09:34.290
Of course, I'm okay anytime

1:09:34.890 --> 1:09:36.490
If I can have the opportunity!

1:09:38.690 --> 1:09:39.490
Is it really okay?

1:09:41.190 --> 1:09:41.790
Of course!

1:09:51.990 --> 1:09:54.990
The following day, Ochi and Yashiro had their game

1:10:08.590 --> 1:10:11.890
Yashiro didn't play an aerial match like yesterday...

1:10:12.990 --> 1:10:14.290
And Ochi did well, too

1:10:15.490 --> 1:10:16.090
But...

1:10:34.990 --> 1:10:35.890
I resign

1:10:41.390 --> 1:10:42.890
End of one fight...

1:10:43.390 --> 1:10:44.990
Is the beginning of the next fight

1:10:46.890 --> 1:10:50.990
This isn't everything, but this isn't the end either

1:10:52.590 --> 1:10:56.290
We're within a long and huge flow...

1:11:03.390 --> 1:11:04.690
That kind of move isn't going to work!

1:11:06.190 --> 1:11:09.090
In this place, instead of protecting.
Waiting for the moment is advantageous

1:11:09.790 --> 1:11:12.890
It's not a good form for me

1:11:13.990 --> 1:11:18.390
Because you keep choosing what you like and dislike, you lost in the Honinbou league, right?

1:11:19.090 --> 1:11:19.790
Hey, Shindou!

1:11:20.290 --> 1:11:23.690
You failed from the second preliminary round in the Honinbou league yourself...

1:11:24.190 --> 1:11:24.990
Kitajima-san...

1:11:25.490 --> 1:11:27.990
There are many other matches, too. You just wait and see!

1:11:28.390 --> 1:11:30.190
I'll catch up to someone like Touya soon!

1:11:30.690 --> 1:11:32.290
Try it if you can!

1:11:32.290 --> 1:11:33.490
Look forward to it!

1:11:33.990 --> 1:11:34.890
There, there...

1:11:35.490 --> 1:11:39.890
Those two are good rivals who are able to lively share their opinions

1:11:40.590 --> 1:11:44.090
Isn't having a good rival something to be thankful about?

1:11:44.990 --> 1:11:47.190
First, it's just enjoyable to play Go with each other

1:11:48.090 --> 1:11:53.590
For me... I have fun playing Go because I have Kitajima-san who is just my match

1:11:53.990 --> 1:11:57.590
As.. Is saying "just my match" impolite to say to Kitajima-san?

1:12:00.490 --> 1:12:01.390
You know.. then..

1:12:02.990 --> 1:12:04.990
God of Go must be lonely

1:12:07.890 --> 1:12:10.990
He won't have any opponents who are equal to himself

1:12:12.790 --> 1:12:14.390
That's an interesting conversation

1:12:15.390 --> 1:12:20.990
Perhaps that's why the God of Go has taught humans how to play Go to advance in it

1:12:22.790 --> 1:12:26.590
In order to bring up a Go player who can be good enough to be his opponent

1:12:34.690 --> 1:12:35.090
Then...

1:12:35.490 --> 1:12:38.990
Even the Go players who lived before, and those Go players who are living now...

1:12:39.890 --> 1:12:43.590
Are all cutting and polishing the stones over and over again for that reason?

1:12:44.090 --> 1:12:45.590
That's it. That's it

1:12:46.090 --> 1:12:49.090
With giving everyone each other's influences

1:12:50.790 --> 1:12:55.090
In that case, it's a huge plan that will take about one million years

1:12:55.690 --> 1:13:01.190
Then, I'm putting in a little contribution to that plan by playing Go

1:13:01.590 --> 1:13:03.690
There's no contribution, no contribution at all!

1:13:03.690 --> 1:13:05.090
Shindou!

1:13:05.090 --> 1:13:06.490
Really,

1:13:07.090 --> 1:13:11.390
Shindou-Kun's opponent these days isn't Akira, but Kitajima-san!

1:13:13.390 --> 1:13:14.090
Let's continue

1:13:15.390 --> 1:13:15.890
Yeah

1:13:39.690 --> 1:13:40.190
Sai

1:13:40.990 --> 1:13:42.190
I'm going to become stronger

1:13:43.990 --> 1:13:46.590
And someday... I'll definitely play...

1:13:47.290 --> 1:13:48.290
The Divine Move!

1:13:55.490 --> 1:13:57.690
The one you continuously pursued...

1:13:58.090 --> 1:13:58.890
The Divine Move!

1:13:59.690 --> 1:14:00.390
Wait!

1:14:00.790 --> 1:14:01.590
Sai!
